# Imported context and explicitly injected queue completion test recovery only.
# No generation job, discovery job, or provider call is executed.
name: Review a recovered context result and handle missing output honestly
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 30 READY THE MAP RUN | setup
keys: Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Build threat model | map-selection
keys: Down Down Down Space Enter
require-live-snap: 20 READY THE MAP RUN | setup-with-context
keys: Down Down Down Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 GENERATE STUDY CONTEXT | context-form
keys: t
type: 5
keys: Enter r
type: 2
keys: Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Draft ready | prepared-map
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE | map-approval
keys: End
require-live-snap: 15 y approve | approval-last
keys: y
require-live-snap: 30 Open approved Map jobs | approved-map
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART complete
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 READY THE MAP RUN | returned-setup
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 CONTEXT JOB RESULT | recovered-result
expect: Inspect generated context
expect: Enter inspects the exact revision
ask: Does returning to Setup reveal the completed result and make inspection the next action, while preserving the exact plan and allowance?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | inspected-result
expect: Alpha
ask: Does Enter open the generated revision for inspection from Setup, with clear selection and Back controls?
keys: v
require-live-snap: 20 CONTEXT DATA FLOW | recovered-diagram
expect: Alpha receiver
resize: 40x12
live-snap: recovered-diagram-40
ask: Does the recovered diagram keep its element, detail and Back controls at the smallest terminal size?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 CHOOSE STUDY CONTEXT | returned-context
keys: a
resize: 120x36
require-live-snap: 20 Context selected for this study | selected-context
expect: Total calls
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 Draft ready | scan-draft
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART selected
ask: Does the next finite scan plan use the selected revision and the same allowance without silently launching scans?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 READY THE MAP RUN | returned-with-scan
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART remove-result
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 CONTEXT JOB RESULT | missing-result
expect: Inspect context job outcome
expect: Context result unavailable
expect-not: Open approved Map jobs
ask: Does missing generated output have an honest explanation and a job-inspection action instead of inviting another launch?
resize: 80x24
live-snap: missing-80
ask: Is the recovery problem and next action readable at 80x24?
resize: 60x20
live-snap: missing-60
ask: Is the recovery explanation reachable with visible paging controls at 60x20?
resize: 40x12
live-snap: missing-40
ask: Does the smallest result view preserve the next action and Back controls?
keys: NPage
live-snap: missing-40-explanation
ask: Is the exact missing-output explanation readable on the next page at 40x12?
keys: NPage
live-snap: missing-40-paged
ask: Can the operator read the missing-result explanation and retained allowance through the advertised paging controls?
resize: 96x89
live-snap: missing-tall
ask: Does the tall view make the recorded plan, result problem and remaining allowance clear?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: missing-wide
ask: Does the wide view keep a comfortable reading width and visible controls?
keys: Enter
resize: 120x36
require-live-snap: 20 Context result unavailable | job-outcome
expect: completed
expect: cost unavailable
expect: separately approved replacement draft
expect-not: L launch
ask: Does inspecting the job preserve its completed state and explain that a replacement requires separate approval?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 15 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | quit-review
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/resume-command.txt
keys: Enter
nav-mode:
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 CONTEXT JOB RESULT | recovered-missing
expect: Inspect context job outcome
expect-not: Open approved Map jobs
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART resumed
ask: Does a fresh no-color session preserve the same unavailable result and allowance, without replacement work or another approval?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 CHOOSE STUDY CONTEXT | back-to-context
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 PLAN A STUDY | back-to-study
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 KUZUSHI | back-to-campaign
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART fail-job
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 CONTEXT JOB RESULT | failed-result
expect: is failed
expect: labeled fixture
expect: refusal) before approving replacement work
expect-not: Open approved Map jobs
ask: Does a failed context job show its recorded reason and inspection action, with no offer to repeat the consumed attempt?
keys: n
require-live-snap: 20 GENERATE STUDY CONTEXT | replacement-draft
expect: Prepare context draft
expect: Total calls: 5
expect: Protected review: 2
ask: Does requesting a new draft preserve spending limits and require preparing and approving new work?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 CHOOSE STUDY CONTEXT | back-from-replacement
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 PLAN A STUDY | leave-study
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 KUZUSHI | returned-campaign
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
